faqs:
- q: Are there companies that help with downsizing in the UK?
  a: Yes. Chayce is a UK downsizing company for older people, based in Northampton. We help you sort and declutter, pack, move and settle in, with one coordinator and fully insured removals. Packages start at {bronze}.
- q: Is there downsizing help near me in Northampton?
  a: 'Yes. Chayce is based on Kingsthorpe Road in Northampton and provides downsizing help for older people across Northamptonshire and the UK: sorting and decluttering, packing, a fully insured removal and settling in, with one coordinator. See our <a href="/elderly-removals-northampton/">Northampton page</a>.'
- q: What does downsizing help for older people include?
  a: Deciding what fits in the smaller home, sorting room by room into keep, sell, donate and let go, careful packing, a fully insured removal and unpacking, depending on your package. Nothing is disposed of without your agreement.
- q: Can you help me downsize my parent&rsquo;s home?
  a: Yes. Moves are often arranged by adult children on a parent&rsquo;s behalf, by phone or video, with your coordinator keeping everyone updated. See <a href="/moving-elderly-parent/">moving an elderly parent</a>.
- q: How much does downsizing help cost in the UK?
  a: Chayce packages start at {bronze} for packing and removals and {silver} for a full-service move with declutter support. A Discovery Consultation costs {discovery}. Final cost depends on property size and the support you need.
- q: How do I start downsizing my home?
  a: Start by deciding where you want to live and roughly when. Then sort belongings room by room into keep, sell, donate and let go. A Discovery Consultation gives you a personalised plan and timeline so you know what to tackle first.
- q: How long does downsizing take?
  a: Most people need three to six months to sort a family home comfortably and time the move around a sale or purchase. Shorter timescales are possible with a fuller-service package.
- q: Should I downsize in retirement?
  a: It can free up money, cut running costs and give you a home that is easier to manage, but it also costs money to move and means leaving a home you know. Weigh the costs, including stamp duty, and take regulated advice on money questions. See our guide on <a href="/blog/when-to-downsize-uk/">when to downsize</a>.
- q: Can you help with sentimental belongings?
  a: Yes. Our coordinators help you decide at your own pace what to keep, pass on or let go, and never push you to make quick decisions.
- q: Do you pack and unpack for older people?
  a: Yes. Packing is included from Bronze Essentials at {bronze}, with boxes labelled by destination room. Unpacking and setting up the new home is included from Silver Comfort at {silver}.
- q: Do you work with my estate agent and solicitor?
  a: Yes. Your coordinator liaises with your estate agent and solicitor, and Gold Prestige adds full solicitor coordination.
- q: Is the removal insured?
  a: Yes. Every Chayce removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit, and the cover is set out in your service agreement before the move begins.
- q: Do you work outside Northampton?
  a: Yes. We are based in Northampton and arrange moves across the whole UK.
